# 💬 Real-Time Chat App

A lightweight, room-based real-time chat application built with **WebSockets**, **React 19**, **TypeScript**, and **Tailwind CSS**. Users can create or join a chat room using a Room ID and exchange messages instantly with others in the same room.

🔗 **Live Demo:** [https://github.com/kiran0094/chatapp](https://github.com/kiran0094/chatapp)

---

## ✨ Features

- 🔗 **Room-based chat** — Join any room using a custom Room ID.
- ⚡ **Real-time messaging** — Messages are delivered instantly via WebSockets.
- 👥 **Multi-user support** — Multiple clients can chat within the same room.
- 💬 **Live message updates** — No page refresh required.
- 🎨 **Responsive UI** — Clean, modern interface styled with Tailwind CSS.
- 🔄 **Persistent WebSocket connection** — Continuous two-way communication between client and server.

---

## 🏗️ Architecture

```
┌──────────────┐
│    Client    │
│  (React 19)  │
│              │
│  Join Room   │
│  Send Message│
└──────┬───────┘
       │
       │ WebSocket (ws)
       ▼
┌────────────────────┐
│   WebSocket Server │
│   (Node.js + ws)   │
│                    │
│  Room Management   │
│  Message Routing   │
└─────────┬──────────┘
          │
          │ Broadcast
          ▼
   ┌───────────────┐
   │ Users in Room │
   └───────────────┘
```

### Room Logic

When a client connects, it joins a room by providing a Room ID. The server maintains an in-memory collection of rooms and their connected clients.

```
Room "general"
 ├── Client 1
 ├── Client 2
 └── Client 3

Room "random"
 ├── Client 4
 └── Client 5
```

Messages sent in a room are broadcast **only** to clients connected to that room.

