## 🛠️ Tech Stack

| Layer        | Technology                              |
|--------------|------------------------------------------|
| **Frontend** | React 19, TypeScript, Vite, Tailwind CSS |
| **Backend**  | Node.js, TypeScript, `ws` (WebSocket)     |
| **Routing**  | React Router DOM v7                      |
| **Build**    | Vite (frontend), `tsc` (backend)         |

---

## 🚀 Getting Started

### Prerequisites

- [Node.js](https://nodejs.org/) (v18+ recommended)
- npm (comes with Node.js)

### 1. Clone the repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/kiran0094/chatapp.git
cd chatapp
```

### 2. Install & run the backend

```bash
cd backend
npm install
npm run dev
```

The WebSocket server will start on **port 8080**.

### 3. Install & run the frontend

Open a new terminal:

```bash
cd frontend
npm install
npm run dev
```

The frontend will start on **http://localhost:5173** (default Vite port).

---

## 💻 Usage

1. Open the app in your browser.
2. Enter a **Room ID** (e.g., `general`, `random`, `team-alpha`).
3. Click **Join Room**.
4. Open the app in another browser tab or device.
5. Enter the **same Room ID**.
6. Start chatting in real time!

---

## 🔌 WebSocket Message Protocol

### Client → Server

| Action      | Payload                                    |
|-------------|--------------------------------------------|
| Join Room   | `{ "type": "join", "payload": { "roomId": "general" } }` |
| Send Chat   | `{ "type": "chat", "payload": { "message": "Hello!" } }` |

### Server → Client

| Event            | Payload                                           |
|------------------|---------------------------------------------------|
| Join Confirmation| `{ "status": "success", "message": "Joined room general" }` |
| Incoming Message | `{ "status": "receiver", "message": "Hello!" }`   |

---

## 🧠 Backend Overview (`backend/src/index.ts`)

The server uses the [`ws`](https://github.com/websockets/ws) library to manage WebSocket connections:

- Maintains an in-memory array of connected users (`allSocket`) with their socket and `roomId`.
- On `"join"`: Adds the client to the specified room.
- On `"chat"`: Finds the sender's room and broadcasts the message to all other clients in that room.
- Tracks active user count.

---

## 🎨 Frontend Overview

- **`App.tsx`** — Manages the global WebSocket connection, handles room join logic, and routes between the landing page (`/`) and the chat room (`/chat`).
- **`pages/chat.tsx`** — Displays messages with distinct styling for sent vs. received messages. Supports sending via button or **Enter key**.

---

## 🔐 Security Considerations

For production use, consider adding:

- ✅ Authentication & authorization
- ✅ Input validation & message size limits
- ✅ Rate limiting to prevent spam
- ✅ WSS (WebSocket Secure) over HTTPS
- ✅ Proper cleanup of disconnected clients
- ✅ Server-side validation of Room IDs

